## Prioritized Requirements Baseline & Acceptance Criteria

### FR-001: Categorized Request Intake

* **Priority:** High
* **Source:** Requester Group
* **Description:** The system shall allow logged-in Requesters to create a new service request by choosing a category and supplying a text description.
* **Acceptance Criteria:** Category dropdown mandatory; text area requires $\ge 15$ chars. Valid submission generates a unique tracking ID and sets status to Open.

### FR-002: Workflow Status Transitions

* **Priority:** High
* **Source:** Field Staff Group
* **Description:** Authorized Staff users shall be able to transition a request's state from Open to In Progress or Resolved.
* **Acceptance Criteria:** Only authenticated Staff/Management can view controls. Appends an immutable audit log entry. Resolving requires a summary note.

### FR-003: Overdue Task Analytics

* **Priority:** Medium
* **Source:** Executive Management
* **Description:** Highlights requests exceeding 48-hour operational SLA timelines.
* **Acceptance Criteria:** Calculates elapsed time = current time minus created time for non-resolved requests. Requests > 48h flagged as Overdue in summary report.

### NFR-001: Query Performance & Response Latency

* **Priority:** High (Quality Guardrail)
* **Description:** Backend maintains sub-2-second response times for data retrieval operations under standard operational loads ($\le 2.0\text{s}$ at 95th percentile under 50 concurrent virtual users).

### NFR-002: Role-Based Authorization Enforcement

* **Priority:** High (System Security)
* **Description:** Server-side authorization checks on all restricted endpoints. Unauthenticated or unauthorized calls rejected with HTTP 401 or 403 status codes.

