## Milestone 3: Construction, Integration, Quality & Release Readiness

### M3 Overview & Administrative Information

* **GitHub Repository URL:** `[https://github.com/bernudup560/Sen381_Virtual_Group_Q.git](https://github.com/bernudup560/Sen381_Virtual_Group_Q.git)`
* **Staging Environment:** Local / Staging Container
* **M3 Release Readiness Status:** CONDITIONALLY READY

### M3 Construction & Configuration Management

All construction followed a strict feature-branch strategy with protected main branch rules requiring at least one peer review per PR. App secrets and connection strings were strictly kept out of version control using .NET User Secrets and environment variable bindings. The UI was overhauled using Bootstrap 5 fluid containers and custom CSS (`site.css`) to ensure accessibility for elderly users with high-contrast elements and large touch targets.

### M3 Automated Verification Suite & CI Quality Gates

A GitHub Actions CI workflow was implemented to trigger on pushes and PRs to main, running automated build and test checks.

* **Equivalence Partitioning & BVA:** Used to test form input validation bounds, text area length limits, and multi-criteria search filtering.
* **Negative & Security Testing:** Verified that unauthenticated users accessing `/Create` are redirected to `/Account/Login`, and BOLA parameter tampering on ticket edits is rejected.
* **End-to-End System Journey:** Verified citizen ticket creation, admin status triage (Submitted > In Progress > Resolved > Closed), and archive retention.

### Performance & Reliability Screening

Conducted a manageable performance check on ticket search filtering and sorting operations under standard local loads. Results confirmed instant response times ($< 200\text{ms}$) under local DOM loading, satisfying NFR-001 within local testing bounds.

